ay be classified as an epithet for Prospero at entity classification time\n   187→5. **Character merging post-processor** - Final cleanup may re-merge characters\n   188→\n   189→### Recommended Next Approach\n   190→\n   191→**CRITICAL: STOP modifying cross-group resolution code - 11 attempts prove the bug is not there.**\n   192→\n   193→1. **Add comprehensive tracing** at the PROPOSER level:\n   194→   - What entities does each proposer extract for \"the mummer\"?\n   195→   - What group does each proposer assign \"the mummer\" to?\n   196→   - Is \"the mummer\" being associated with Prospero BEFORE consensus runs?\n   197→\n   198→2. **Examine the NER extraction stage** in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/`:\n   199→   - How does spaCy classify \"the mummer\"?\n   200→   - Is coreference resolution linking \"the mummer\" to \"Prospero\"?\n   201→\n   202→3. **Add a DEBUG environment variable** to dump intermediate state:\n   203→   - Proposer outputs before consensus\n   204→   - Consensus input (what pairs are being considered)\n   205→   - Cross-group resolution input (what groups exist)\n   206→\n   207→4. **Consider inverting the problem**:\n   208→   - Since the summary pipeline correctly identifies 2 characters, can we use the summary output to VALIDATE/CORRECT character extraction?\n   209→   - Add a post-processing step: \"If the chapter summary mentions character X as distinct from character Y, they should NOT be merged\"\n   210→\n   211→## Fix History\n   212→\n   213→### Attempt 12 Fixes Applied\n   214→1. **Increased mention context window to 250** (src/agents/config.py line 72)\n   215→   - Changed `character_mention_context_chars` from 200 -> 250 characters\n   216→   - Root cause: Death scene is 221 chars long, 200-char window was splitting the evidence\n   217→   - Smoke test: ✅ PASS - \"the mummer\" now separate from \"the Prince Prospero\"\n   218→   - Modified: src/agents/config.py\n   219→\n   220→### Attempt 11 Fixes Applied\n   221→1. **